# Named people at holdings: two of territory's built people get topics.

conv named.redhand.tollman
for named:redhand/toll_man
topic "Who painted the red hand?"
prio world
voice redhand

node start
  say The boss did. On the shutter of Rudi's garage, at the crossroads, the day the garage changed hands. Rudi had the diesel, the Janda boys had the lorry, the boss had the book.
  say The boss said the hand means stop. Every toll on every road has one now, painted on the barrier. Rudi was bitten.
  > @really Was he, though? Really bitten? -> really
  > @toll How's the toll been today? -> toll
  > @other Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node really
  say Rudi was bitten.
  > @back1 Right. Let me ask something else. -> hub

node toll
  say Good. A tin a car on this road, more if you look like you can afford it. Tins mostly, fuel when we're lucky, the odd wedding ring. All of it goes in the book, and the boss takes a cut.
  say Bastion paid in bullets once. We counted that as a tip. Then we counted them, because we count everything.
  > @back2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv named.bastion.sentry
for named:bastion/sentry
topic "What's this roll everyone talks about?"
prio world
voice bastion

node start
  say When the night watch is set, the sergeant reads the whole roster out loud. Every name on the post. The living answer for themselves: here.
  say For each of the dead, the whole post answers together. Here. It gets longer every week. Command never answers us. So we answer for each other.
  > @hear Can I listen to it tonight? -> hear
  > @how How long does it take now? -> how
  > @road I'll walk the road. Back in two hours. -> road   if !promise:sentry.road@here.visit & !kept:sentry.road@here.visit & !broke:sentry.road@here.visit   do promise:sentry.road@here.visit:2h
  > @other2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node hear
  say? night :: You're hearing it now. Stand still, hat off, mouth shut. If the sergeant looks at you, you're furniture.
  say Twenty-thirty, at the wire. Stand outside it, hat off. Don't answer for anyone. You haven't earned anyone yet.
  > @back3 Understood. I'll be there. -> hub

node road
  say Nobody comes back and says. They walk off down that road and that's the last line in the log: departed, eastbound, no further contact. Prove me wrong.
  say Two hours. Then I log you as gone, and I don't enjoy it, and I do it anyway.
  > @back5 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node how
  say Longer than the call to Command, which takes ten seconds and gets static. Shorter than it should be. We lost the count of the dead around Day nine.
  say No. That's not true. We know the count, to the man. We just don't say it out loud. The roll says it for us.
  > @back4 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

conv named.bastion.sentry_back
for named:bastion/sentry
when kept:sentry.road@here.visit
greet
once
prio reaction
voice bastion

node start
  say? kept:sentry.road@here.visit :: You came back. Most don't. I'll log the road as walked, with your name against it. First good line in this log all week.

conv named.bastion.sentry_gone
for named:bastion/sentry
when broke:sentry.road@here.visit
greet
once
prio reaction
voice bastion

node start
  say? broke:sentry.road@here.visit :: Logged you as gone, two hours after you said. Glad to rub it out. It's the only rubbing out we ever get to do on this post.
